<section
  class="nit nit-problem nit-section"
  aria-labelledby="nit-problem-heading"
>
  <div class="nit-container nit-problem__inner nit-problem__inner--start">
    <div class="nit-problem__media nit-reveal"><div class="nit-media" style="--nit-ratio: 4/5"><div class="nit-media__placeholder">
      <p class="nit-label nit-media__slot">problem-interior</p>
      <p class="nit-media__shot nit-small">Footwell and seat rail, low natural light, grit visible in the carpet weave</p>
      <p class="nit-label nit-media__dims nit-nums">1400 &#215; 1750 &middot; 4:5</p>
    </div></div>
</div>

    <div class="nit-problem__copy"><p class="nit-label nit-reveal">Why it is awkward</p><h2 class="nit-h1 nit-problem__heading nit-reveal" id="nit-problem-heading">
        A car interior is not a small room
      </h2><div class="nit-body nit-muted nit-problem__body nit-reveal">
          <p>It is a set of narrow gaps arranged around furniture that does not move. Household vacuums are built for open floors, and the places a car actually gets dirty are the places a full-size head cannot reach.</p>
        </div><ul class="nit-problem__points" role="list" data-nit-stagger><li class="nit-problem__point nit-reveal" >
              <p class="nit-label nit-problem__point-key">Geometry</p>
              <p class="nit-small nit-problem__point-text">Seat rails, belt anchors and the channel between seat and console are all narrower than a standard vacuum head.</p>
            </li><li class="nit-problem__point nit-reveal" >
              <p class="nit-label nit-problem__point-key">Power</p>
              <p class="nit-small nit-problem__point-text">Cars are parked where sockets are not. A mains lead reaches the driveway or it does not reach at all.</p>
            </li><li class="nit-problem__point nit-reveal" >
              <p class="nit-label nit-problem__point-key">Debris</p>
              <p class="nit-small nit-problem__point-text">Grit and pet hair work into the weave rather than sitting on it, so suction has to lift rather than sweep.</p>
            </li></ul></div>
  </div>
</section>

